The system service is giving you a error from the probe of the
arguments.  I'd check either the line:

	terminal.dsc$a_pointer = device_name;

and make it:

	terminal.dsc$a_pointer = &device_name[];

or the line:

	status = sys$assign(terminal, &user_input_chan, 0, 0);

and make it:

	status = sys$assign(&terminal, &user_input_chan, 0, 0);

I always get into trouble on how C decides what to do when passing
structures.


