  The problem was the latter one I think.  In VMS C, structures are passed
by copy in the argument list.  sys$assign, needs a pointer to the descriptor
so you need &terminal in the SYS$ASSIGN.  The fudging of the descriptor
is O.K. since array names without subscripts can be treated as pointers to
their contents.  By the way, more standard and portable than what you showed
is:

   terminal.dsc$a_pointer = &device_name[0];

Which should also work.
